  "notes": "Sources: Änderung der Prüfungsordnung Bachelor Technische Informatik (Verkündungsblatt 12/2026, in force 01.10.2026), Modulkatalog Technische Informatik Bachelor WS 2026/27 (Stand 07.09.2026), Studienverlaufsplan v8.7.2026. Module codes are made up for this preset; LUH publishes none. Gesamtnote per PO § 20 Abs. 3: LP-weighted mean of all graded modules, truncated after the first decimal. Per § 20 Abs. 1-2 only the best elective modules needed for 180 LP count: 180 - 149 fixed LP - 3 LP Studium Generale = 28 LP from the two Vertiefung areas, at least 10 LP from each (Anlage 1.6/1.7). This assumes 3 LP Studium Generale; more Studium Generale lowers the limit. Anlage 1 allows up to 20 LP per Vertiefung area; the Modulkatalog states 10-15 LP. Composite module grades (§ 20 Abs. 5, e.g. Bachelorarbeit 80 % thesis and 20 % presentation) are truncated means, so every tenth from 1.0 to 4.0 is allowed. Proseminar is one placeholder for any Proseminar in the catalog. Studium Generale is modelled as one 3 LP module (3-6 LP allowed). Elective lists contain the Vertiefung modules offered in the WS 2026/27 catalog, without greyed-out modules and without the \"Aktuelle Themen\" placeholders used for external credits. Einführung in die Informatik applies to students starting from 01.10.2025. Attempts per § 14 Abs. 1: a failed Prüfungsleistung can be repeated twice (3 attempts), the Bachelorarbeit once (2 attempts); passed exams cannot be retaken. § 14 Abs. 1 Satz 3 also limits Studienarbeiten to one repetition; the programme lists none. A failed Klausur in the last attempt is followed by an Ergänzungsprüfung that can raise it to 4.0 at most (§ 14 Abs. 4). Not modelled yet: Prädikat \"mit Auszeichnung\" (§ 20 Abs. 4). Withdrawal deadline per § 15 Abs. 2: Klausuren until 7 days before the exam; mündliche Prüfungen until 1 day before. The preset uses the Klausur rule.",
